  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A$ and $B$ be two square matrices of order 3 and $A B=O_{3}$, where $O_{3}$ denotes the null matrix of order 3. Then,"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "must be $A=O_{3}, B=O_{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "if $A \\neq O_{3}$, must be $B \\neq O$,",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "if $A=O_{3}$. must be $B \\neq O_{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "may be $A \\neq O_{3} . B \\neq O_{3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, product of two non-null matrix can be a null matrix.\r\nTherefore, may be\r\n$$\r\nA \\neq O_{3}, B \\neq O_{3}\r\n$$"
  }
}